 To specify which [configuration file](CONFIGURATION.md) to load, use the `--config.file` flag.
 
+To validate a configuration file without starting the exporter, use the `--config.check` flag. Besides parsing the configuration, this also checks that the local files it references (such as `body_file`, TLS `ca_file`/`cert_file`/`key_file`, and credential files) exist and are readable. No network requests are made.
